# UI (views and component templates)

- CSS: **Tailwind CSS 4** + **DaisyUI 5**. Prefer using DaisyUI components/utilities when it improves consistency, and Tailwind utilities for layout/spacing.
- **Dark mode:** every new/changed template must work with DaisyUI themes (including `dark`). Prefer semantic tokens (`bg-base-100`, `bg-base-200`, `text-base-content`, `border-base-200`, `text-primary`, `hover:bg-base-200`) over raw palette colors (`text-gray-900`, `bg-white`, `hover:bg-gray-50`, `text-dark-blue`) unless a `dark:` variant is also provided.
- Prefer Turbo + Stimulus over bespoke JS. Keep JS minimal and data-attribute-driven.
- DRY: prefer **ViewComponent** with `--sidecar` (template + YAML beside the Ruby class); helpers next; partials only when a component is not a good fit.
- Icons: **FontAwesome** when icons are needed (see `package.json`).
- Accessibility & responsive: semantic HTML, labels, focus, spacing; avoid layouts that break Turbo or mobile tap targets.
- Hotwire Native: avoid heavy client-only navigation patterns; favor Turbo and progressive enhancement.
- Security: avoid inline scripts in views (XSS and maintainability).
